      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-ink mb-8 tracking-tight mt-16 border-t border-hairline pt-16">
        7. Dangerous Myths About Weight, Obesity, and Health
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-body mb-8">
        The monstrous multibillion-dollar industry of extreme fad diets and fat-burning supplements has, for profit, perpetuated atrocious myths that terribly confuse the population, discourage, and ultimately impede the progress of millions of well-intentioned people. Let's scientifically and forever debunk the most destructive ones, firmly relying on modern clinical evidence.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <!-- Myth 1 -->
        <div class="bg-red-50/50 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-red-100 relative">
          <div class="absolute -top-4 -left-4 w-12 h-12 bg-red-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-red-600 text-2xl font-bold">❌</div>
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-4 mt-2">Myth:"Carbohydrates, especially at night, block fat burning and make you instantly fat."</h4>
          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
            <strong>False. The Scientific Reality:</strong> No isolated macronutrient possesses the magical or esoteric power to create adipose tissue out of absolute nothingness, breaking elementary physics. The famous pseudoscientific"carbohydrate-insulin" model of obesity development has been extensively and systematically debunked in a humiliating manner in multiple and rigorous isolated and highly controlled metabolic trials in closed metabolic wards. The chronic, prolonged, and inexcusable excess of total ingested calories (regardless of their dietary origin) is the sole and exclusive biological culprit that your body will use to synthesize and store excess surplus energy in the form of fat cells (adipocytes). In fact, complex carbohydrates (like whole oatmeal, rice, and nutritious tubers like potatoes) are absolutely the preferred and fastest-access fuel for your demanding brain and muscles during truly intense physical training.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Myth 2 -->
        <div class="bg-red-50/50 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-red-100 relative">
          <div class="absolute -top-4 -left-4 w-12 h-12 bg-red-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-red-600 text-2xl font-bold">❌</div>
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-4 mt-2">Myth:"You can do specific and localized repetitive exercises to quickly burn stubborn belly fat."</h4>
          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
            <strong>False. The Scientific Reality:</strong> Medically known as the delusion of"spot reduction," this is one of the oldest and most profitable commercial myths in teleshopping. You can stoically subject yourself to methodically performing a thousand daily crunches or torturous abdominal exercises; you will undoubtedly immensely hypertrophy and strengthen the powerful wall of underlying core muscle tissue that is under your skin, but you will never, under any natural biological circumstance, magically make your body oxidize, or"burn," preferentially that stubborn layer of fat tissue located right above the worked area. Your immutable personal genetic map, heredity, and your endogenous hormonal profile dictate in what strict and predetermined biological order your body is forced to mobilize fatty acids in pure systemic and global biochemical response to a severe generalized caloric deficit sustained over the long term.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Myth 3 -->
        <div class="bg-red-50/50 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-red-100 relative md:col-span-2">
          <div class="absolute -top-4 -left-4 w-12 h-12 bg-red-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-red-600 text-2xl font-bold">❌</div>
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-4 mt-2">Myth:"Sweating excessively with neoprene belts on treadmills unequivocally equates to losing and melting a large amount of body fat."</h4>
          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
            <strong>False. The Scientific Reality:</strong> Absurdly wrapping your body like a gift in suffocating plastics to train, wearing double thermal sweatshirts in summer, or simply spending three arduous hours straight in the suffocating heat of a sauna will never burn a single extra gram of body fat on its own. Sweat is, plain and simple, the efficient, rudimentary, and ancient biological mechanism of extreme emergency thermoregulation of your primary system, evolutionarily designed to rapidly cool the skin through evaporation and prevent your certain death from critical organ overheating. This fluid expelled through your pores is composed almost exclusively of water and tiny traces of basic vital electrolytes (like sodium and potassium). The exciting and rapid acute drop in magical weight that you emotionally see momentarily reflected on the cold scale in the locker room right after leaving the sauna is the purest acute dehydration; there is no magic; every milligram of this lost"sweated weight" will return, aggressively and completely recovering, instantaneously and obligatorily the exact second you simply properly rehydrate your cells by drinking a simple and necessary glass of water.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
